# Pairs with NoKeyLost. Reproduces the resize snapshot after #4506 and #4566,
# and before #4522's resize fix (#4629): the snapshot's sweep resolves a bucket of a
# decided saga at the destination with the committed-values backstop at a fresh
# dominating stamp (carryOriginalStamps: false), instead of carrying it. A later
# write the snapshot already copied to R is overwritten.
MODULE: NoKeyLostSnapshotResolvesAtFreshStamp
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the snapshot resolves a decided saga's bucket on R at a fresh stamp, overwriting a later write already copied
PERTURBS: SnapCopy

--- FIND
                 THEN LWW(row[R][s][k], row[T][s][k]) ELSE row[x][s][k]]]]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a decided saga's bucket is resolved on R at a fresh stamp.
                 THEN IF dec = "committed" /\ pend[T][s][k] # "none" THEN FreshV
                      ELSE LWW(row[R][s][k], row[T][s][k])
                 ELSE row[x][s][k]]]]
--- END

--- FIND
                 IF x = R /\ s \in rzShards /\ pend[R][s][k] = "none"
--- REPLACE
                 IF x = R /\ s \in rzShards /\ pend[R][s][k] = "none" /\ dec # "committed"
--- END